    "hsd_section_diamond_params_pV6ngX": {
      "type": "hsd-section-diamond-params",
      "blocks": {
        "hsd_4c_item_hffViP": {
          "type": "hsd-4c-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Diamond Size:",
            "content": "{carat}",
            "intro": "",
            "learn_more_link": "",
            "learn_more_text": "Learn More",
            "description": "<p>The carat denotes the weight of a diamond, often misunderstood as a measure of size. One carat equals 200 milligrams or 0.2 grams. The scale below demonstrates the typical relationship between diamond sizes and increasing carat weights, but it's important to note that each diamond is inherently unique.</p>",
            "intro_position_left": 2,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_4Cs_of_Your_Diamond_Diamond_Size.webp"
          }
        },
        "hsd_4c_item_trBwVj": {
          "type": "hsd-4c-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Color",
            "content": "{color}",
            "intro": "",
            "learn_more_link": "",
            "learn_more_text": "Learn More",
            "description": "<p>Color in a diamond refers to its inherent hue, which remains unchanged over time. Diamonds with less color, known as colorless diamonds, permit more light to pass through them, resulting in increased sparkle and fire. When light enters a diamond, it refracts and disperses, creating colorful flashes known as fire, which adds to the diamond's allure.</p>",
            "intro_position_left": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_4Cs_of_Your_Diamond_Diamond_Color.webp"
          }
        },
        "hsd_4c_item_rmTRrG": {
          "type": "hsd-4c-item",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Cut",
            "content": "{cut}",
            "intro": "",
            "learn_more_link": "",
            "learn_more_text": "Learn More",
            "description": "<p>The cut of a diamond encompasses its angles, proportions, depth, and width, along with the uniformity of its facets. This intricate aspect of a diamond influences its overall beauty, as it dictates how effectively the diamond reflects and refracts light. The craftsmanship involved in cutting a diamond significantly impacts its brilliance and sparkle.</p>",
            "intro_position_left": 10,
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/The_4Cs_of_Your_Diamond_Diamond_Cut.webp"
          }
        },
        "hsd_4c_item_XFamL8": {
